  "notes": "This leaf, numbered 2 (pencil 4), begins in mid-parenthesis with a proposed criterion of “non sauvagerie” of γ. It reduces to the unramified case by removing the finite ramification set. The text warns that finite-order translations on C* and U×U can be isotopic to the identity without being the identity. Proposition 2 excludes this for oriented finite-type anabelian surfaces (negative compactly supported Euler characteristic). The proof starts by reducing to a connected component and says that trivial action on homologie H₁, with the inserted qualification p.ex. on coefficients, is enough. The proof continues beyond the page.\n\nThe visible invariant is homology, not H’s cohomology; the small inserted index is lower than H’s baseline, read H₁ with medium confidence. The loop-descending automorphism glyph is read γ throughout the five occurrences, matching its forked upper strokes rather than the conventional choice of σ. The source retains masculine égaux after translations. The singular restriction, short cpte and néc., and des trous are preserved. No date appears.",
